</ul><h1>Big Name</h1><p>Russell, thank you for meeting with us. This is a subject of the utmost importance, so the board has decided to speak through a single mouthpiece–me, in this case–to ensure we keep on topic.</p>
<p>You see, it has come to our attention, Russell, that you have partaken in a series of extramarital affairs. Now, please, before you deny or attempt to scold us for overstepping, know that we, the members of the board, have varying levels of tolerance for such immorality.</p>
<p>The issue, however, is that we fear many, if not all, of these affair partners to be spies.</p>
<p>Just to read a few names our private investigator uncovered: JoAnna Mars, Patricia Reese, Henrietta Hershey, Olivia Whitman, LeAnne Nestle. And I could go on. Seriously, Russell, did none of these strike you as the least bit concerning?</p>
<p>But of course, what worries us more is what our investigators uncovered regarding topics discussed, and, moreover, your readiness to divulge them.</p>
<p>For example, in May, as you and one of these partners drank martinis at a cocktail bar, our PI overheard you speaking of how you managed to devise a chocolate that hardens so rapidly. I’ll admit that those of us on the board, when reading the report, prayed this was innuendo. But no. You were explaining, in depth, your formula for chocolate. What’s more, you didn’t seem to be bothered that your date wrote everything down on a napkin. In fact, according to our PI, you even drew some diagrams for her.</p>
<p>Similar trade secrets–by which I mean, the very pillars upon which the Russell Stover empire has been built–were freely spoken. The secret to our caramel. How we manage to get our marshmallow filling to have such a pillowy soft mouthfeel without being overly chewy and sticky to the teeth. Our various seasonal offerings. All of it, blathered about with little provocation.</p>
<p>And yet, somehow, these admissions to our American competitors are perhaps the least concerning development uncovered.</p>
<p>We have reason to believe that you carried out an affair with a foreigner, as well. A Swiss national. Miss Sofia Lindt. Does this ring a bell?</p>
<p>I can tell by your hesitation it does. Russell, this is very damning news. For we have reason to believe that she seeks not to know how we do what we do, but rather to set in motion a plan that ends with her own family’s chocolate company taking ownership of our brand in the distant future.</p>
<p>So, do you have anything to say for yourself?</p>
<p>Really? That’s it? “Nuh-oh, no I didn’t”?</p>
<p>Well, it’s a compelling argument. Meeting adjourned.</p>